                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s8IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>سوره الفاتحه [...] ايات مكيه \ بسم اللـه الرحمن الرحيم , الحمد لله رب العلمين<note>Part of the sūra heading smudged. </note>
                     </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#16v">-16v</locus>وَلَا تُسْئَلُوْنَ عَمَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ</explicit>
                     <note>1:1-2:141. Curve of final nūn-s, sīn-s and yā'-s semi-circular; curve of final ḥā'-s as well. Different ways to complete words at the end of a line. Among them, incomplete words, often left without diacritic and vocalization, rewritten in full on the following line. Use of hā’ for intahā’ to fill out the line (8r, 9r). Sūrat al-Fātiḥa not vocalized. Red triple commas as verse markers. Ḥizb marker in red on fol. 9r. Catchwords written by another hand.</note>
                     <note/>
                  </msItem>
